From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 1 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lib: gunzip: make gunzip() weak

The K230 provides a gunzip() that decompresses on the UGZIP hardware
block and falls back to software zlib. Make the generic gunzip() weak
so that SoC code can override it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 lib/gunzip.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/gunzip.c b/lib/gunzip.c
index a05dcde9..011c9ec8 100644
--- a/lib/gunzip.c
+++ b/lib/gunzip.c
@@ -72,7 +72,9 @@ __rcode int gzip_parse_header(const unsigned char *src, unsigned long len)
 	return i;
 }
 
-__rcode int gunzip(void *dst, int dstlen, unsigned char *src, unsigned long *lenp)
+/* Weak so that arch/riscv/cpu/k230/unzip.c can decompress in hardware. */
+__weak __rcode int gunzip(void *dst, int dstlen, unsigned char *src,
+			  unsigned long *lenp)
 {
 	int offset = gzip_parse_header(src, *lenp);
 
-- 
2.43.0

